WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:10.652
- (Michael) Hey Wisecrack, Michael here,&nbsp;and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.652 --> 00:00:14.320
today we’re talking about The Boys. The show is&nbsp;
sadistic and hilarious, and has plenty to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.360
about the superhero genre and modern-day America.&nbsp;
But as we watched season two, we kept coming back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.120
to one question: Are any of these characters for&nbsp;
real? When Stormfront or Billy or Homelander talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:31.200
about things they ostensibly care about, are they&nbsp;
just faking it? And if so - why all the posturing?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.720
Let’s find out in this Wisecrack Edition on The&nbsp;
Boys Season 2: and of course spoilers ahead&nbsp;

00:01:32.226 --> 00:01:37.520
- (Michael) And now for a quick recap: The&nbsp;
Boys is the story of one Billy Butcher and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.320
his crew of vigilante misfits who are trying&nbsp;
to take down the Vought Corporation - a very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:47.600
evil company that employs and contracts out&nbsp;
the services of, often evil, superheroes.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:51.495
- (Homelander) What happens&nbsp;
if, oh I don't know, I do this.&nbsp;

00:01:51.495 --> 00:01:53.120
(Screaming)
- (Homelander)&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.920
And now you're just another&nbsp;
useless ******* blind guy.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.360
- (Michael) It’s important to note&nbsp;
that these superheroes aren't some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.400
“happy accident” - RIP to Bob Ross - but&nbsp;
the result of Vought’s very secretive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.360
definitely illegal medical experiments on&nbsp;
children. The Boys try to expose Vought and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.160
save Billy’s wife and her child from their&nbsp;
head-supe - Homelander.&nbsp;Season Two also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:20.080
introduces the latest Vought hero Stormfront,&nbsp;
who turns out to be an actual century-old Nazi.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.000
- (Stormfront) Heinrich&nbsp;
Himmler... he was a lovely dancer.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.720
- (Michael) If it seems like The Boys is full&nbsp;
of people espousing disingenuous politics and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.280
posturing for the cameras, it’s because the&nbsp;
show goes to great lengths to show us how almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.800
every character is constantly performing.&nbsp;&nbsp;
After all, it’s not enough to simply be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.440
hero in this world, you have to play a&nbsp;
hero too.&nbsp;Superheroes star in movies:

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.920
- (Adam) Title card: Dawn of the Seven!

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.384
- (Michael) Go on talk show circuits -

00:02:47.384 --> 00:02:49.040
- (Host) Stormfront, congrats on The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.120
Seven. Are you excited to be here as I am?
- (Stormfront) I don't know! I don't think so!

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.400
- (Michael) And even give those lame&nbsp;
midnight religious infomercials.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.000
- (The Deep) But thanks to&nbsp;
the Church of the Collective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.840
I now know the type of man I want&nbsp;
to be. Hey dude - that's not cool.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.320
- (Michael) Heck, even when they’re not on the&nbsp;
screen, they worry about public approval ratings

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.760
- (Homelander) So what, I'm down&nbsp;
a point? Point and a half? Two?

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.200
- (Michael) And fastidiously try to&nbsp;
keep their “personal” selves in check.&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.360
- (Stormfront) Oh my god everyone&nbsp;
is so fucking stage managed. Life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.320
isn’t actually a PR strategy!&nbsp;
You can say what you think!&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.480
- (Michael) And it’s not just our superheroes&nbsp;
who are constantly putting on a show.&nbsp;Whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:31.680
it’s Becca playing house with a sociopathic&nbsp;
superman, or Congresswoman Victoria Neuman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:38.000
whipping her base into a frenzy, every character&nbsp;
seems to put on a mask at one time or another. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.960
here’s the question, Wisecrack: What do you think&nbsp;
happens when these deliberate performances collide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:48.560
with hot-button, social issues?&nbsp; Well, we’ve got&nbsp;
a term for you: virtue signaling.&nbsp;Now before you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:53.520
smash that dislike button - hear me out.&nbsp;Virtue&nbsp;
signaling is a term that gets thrown around to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.560
suggest that people are disingenuously engaging&nbsp;
with social issues not out of genuine concern but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.200
to promote their own-self image.&nbsp; While it’s&nbsp;
certainly a real phenomenon, it’s basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:08.560
become a catch-all term to call anyone who cares&nbsp;
about anything a fraud. One might say that even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.520
my discussion of virtue signaling is in itself&nbsp;
some kind of signal of virtue about how wise I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:19.120
in an effort to make Wisecrack seem “tres woke”.&nbsp;
And then if you get mad at that and tweet about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:25.280
it, your righteous indignation could itself be&nbsp;
some virtue signaling to your impassioned fans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:31.280
The point is, it’s very easy to call just about&nbsp;
anything virtue signaling -- and it’s also often,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:36.320
but not always, a lazy and incoherent&nbsp;
argument.&nbsp;And it’s confusing because we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:41.120
live in a world where we don’t trust anyone&nbsp;
to stand for anything for the right reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:46.720
And The Boys takes this confusion head on.&nbsp;
The Boys is centrally concerned *not* with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:51.440
how ordinary people display their support&nbsp;
of social issues, but how corporations do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:56.800
In turn, it explores how ordinary people end&nbsp;
up consuming information about those ideas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:02.000
In Season One, for instance, Vought rebrands&nbsp;
their hero, Starlight, as a feminist icon.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.200
- She transforms!
- Embraces her feminine strengths!&nbsp;

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.840
- Good bye yellow brick road!
- And hello Starlight!

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:15.040
- (Michael) Except well, their brand of “female&nbsp;
empowerment through sexuality” isn’t exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:20.000
what the budding superhero had in mind. Vought&nbsp;
doesn’t care - they’re more concerned with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:25.040
image of an empowered woman that people can also&nbsp;
ogle than, you know, actually empowering anyone.&nbsp;

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:32.640
- Most importantly it tells a story. Of your&nbsp;
transformation. Of what you're going through.&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.800
- (Starlight) How exactly do you&nbsp;
know what I'm going through? Exactly?

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.600
- (Michael) A.K.A. - virtue signaling - the&nbsp;
Starlight rebranding helps their bottom line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:45.920
rather than any “feminist” cause. A&nbsp;
similar conflict happens in season 2:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.320
Homelander maliciously outs Queen Maeve:

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.748
- (Maria Menounos) Who in The Seven is gay?
- (Homelander) Queen Maeve.

00:05:51.748 --> 00:05:56.400
- (Michael) Revealing her ex-girlfriend whom Maeve&nbsp;
is then forced to pretend is her current lover.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:01.520
Vought reimagines Maeve’s forced-outing in their&nbsp;
film Dawn of the Seven as a “wholesome” coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:06.080
out story, complete with a cliched love interest&nbsp;
in the form of a counterculture, computer hacker.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.280
- (Queen Maeve) I’m afraid to...&nbsp;
to show the world who I am.&nbsp;

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.600
- (Hacker) Yeah, so who are&nbsp;
you, Meave?” - (Maeve) I’m gay.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:16.160
- (Michael) After establishing&nbsp;
Maeve as a queer icon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.960
Vought capitalizes on it to sell shit like this:

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:23.840
- (Narrator) Brave Maeve Pride Bars. Because&nbsp;
you can’t be proud on an empty stomach.&nbsp;

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:28.000
- (Michael) It’s worth noting that,&nbsp;
while Maeve bars are sadly fictitious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:32.800
this whole “using someone’s identity for&nbsp;
profit” is a fairly common advertising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:38.640
strategy. While your head of digital marketing may&nbsp;
genuinely care about, say, racism, their message&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:43.120
is still getting filtered through the lens of&nbsp;&nbsp;
“what’s going to make us money.”&nbsp; As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:48.720
most companies only support social issues after&nbsp;
they become massively popular and therefore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:53.520
safe. Like how shampoo conglomerate L’Oreal&nbsp;
posted about “standing with the black community”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:58.720
this summer, despite, oh right, apparently&nbsp;
ending their partnership with a model in 2017&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:03.920
because she spoke out against the white supremacy.&nbsp;
And filtering social issues through the lens of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:09.760
profit isn’t just massively annoying, it can&nbsp;
actively harm people. Take Maeve’s sexuality.&nbsp;

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:11.680
- (Elena) You know Maeve is&nbsp;
bi, right?” - (Ashley) Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:15.200
you know what? I just feel like lesbian is a&nbsp;
bit of an easier sell.&nbsp;A bit more cut and dry.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:19.120
- (Michael) Clearly, Vought’s preoccupation&nbsp;
with gay rights is just another sales tactic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.560
not an earnest means of “celebrating”&nbsp;
Maeve for who she actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:27.040
is.&nbsp;The company then tries to overhaul the&nbsp;
image of Maeve’s pretend partner, Elena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:31.440
so she can better conform to the stereotype&nbsp;
of “what a lesbian should look like.”&nbsp;

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.080
- (Elena) That looks like menswear.
- (Seth) Peer Research shows that two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.960
feminine women in a relationship&nbsp;
sends a problematic message.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:40.560
- (Michael) This is the danger of virtue&nbsp;
signaling as marketing strategy - it puts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.760
a corporate-friendly face on social causes,&nbsp;
thus obscuring the actual reality. People are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:50.560
then bombarded with images that reinforce the&nbsp;
big business version of reality. And this sort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:56.080
of corporate “do-gooding” often provides a useful&nbsp;
and deliberate distraction from a given business’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:02.160
less savory practices - this is well documented in&nbsp;
Fran Hawthorne’s&nbsp;“Ethical Chic”. In Vought’s case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.200
all the feminism and gay pride distracts people&nbsp;
from the reality that the company is a private&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:12.400
military contractor with a less-than-stellar&nbsp;
human rights record.&nbsp;In this way, we might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:17.920
better appreciate The Boys’ most glorious&nbsp;
jab at Marvel. For context -- In season 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:23.440
Vought is going all in on female empowerment&nbsp;
with their new PR campaign, “girls get it done.”

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.920
- (Reporter) Can you tell us a&nbsp;
little about "Girls get it done"?&nbsp;

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.200
("Girls Get it Done" repeated by various speakers)

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:33.040
- (Michael) The idea is that since there have&nbsp;
never been three women in the Seven before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:38.320
now’s the time to cash in on, not being sexist&nbsp;
anymore? But for all the congratulatory talk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:42.160
female empowerment is pretty much&nbsp;
the exact opposite of what Vought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:46.240
is actually about. For starters, it’s&nbsp;
newest film, the Dawn of the Seven,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:49.840
isn’t exactly concerned with portraying&nbsp;
realistic female characters.&nbsp;

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:53.200
- (Stormfront) You write women as either&nbsp;
unknowable Hitchcock bitches or Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:57.120
Bay fuck dolls. I mean I get that a life time&nbsp;
of jerking off to Transformers didn't exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.560
make you popular with the ladies,&nbsp;
but, a little effort would be nice.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.920
- (Michael) That’s a literal nazi saying&nbsp;
this.&nbsp; And it’s not like the company has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:09.040
embraced girl power off the screen either -&nbsp;
recall our coerced-into-spandex Starlight.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.840
- (Starlight) I'm fine with my old outfit.
- (Madelyn) We're not. &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:16.960
- (Michael) All of which brings us to THAT Marvel&nbsp;
scene. To summarize, there is one very notable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:21.840
moment in Avengers Endgame when Peter Parker&nbsp;
asks Captain Marvel how she plans to get past the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:27.440
incoming onslaught of badmen. In response,&nbsp;
the Scarlet Witch and Okoye pop in and say:

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:30.720
- (Scarlet Witch) Don’t worry -
- (Okoya) She’s got help.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:35.840
- (Michael) As more female heroes swoop in to&nbsp;
assist our hero. When I saw it, tons of kids went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:41.120
apeshit because Marvel was finally letting their&nbsp;
female heroes shine.&nbsp;But for more jaded adults,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:46.320
this all felt a little forced, exactly the kind&nbsp;
of “corporate feminism” that we’ve become wary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:51.440
of. And The Boys, seems to agree, mimicking&nbsp;
Marvel’s scene in the Dawn of the Seven.&nbsp;

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.720
- (Hacker) How are you gonna&nbsp;
get through all of them&nbsp;

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.120
- (Starlight) Don't worry -
- (Stormfront) Girls get it done!&nbsp;

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:02.240
- (Michael) Much like Vought celebrates their&nbsp;
“girls get it done” after years of being a total&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:07.360
boys club, Marvel’s scene is a weird victory&nbsp;
lap for a company that waited a whole decade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:12.400
before putting out its first standalone female&nbsp;
superhero film, Captain Marvel -- which also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:16.800
happens to be a movie that many have called a&nbsp;
thinly-veiled recruitment tool for the Air Force.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:17.840
- (Brie Larson) You're so cool.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:23.360
- (Michael) And that’s not by accident:&nbsp;
the US Military has often exerted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:28.080
editorial influence over movies like Top Gun&nbsp;
or Captain Marvel in exchange for access to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.360
sick tanks and planes The result? A scrappy&nbsp;
but not too rough-around-the-edges hero who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.520
can be turned both into a toy line and&nbsp;
an advertisement for the US military.

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:41.600
- (Brie Larson) That spirit of her, that&nbsp;
sense of humor, mixed with total capability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:45.440
in whatever challenge comes her way is&nbsp;
really what Air Force pilots are like.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:47.520
- (Michael) The kind of hero who would never,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:50.320
ever do something like kick a&nbsp;
person while they’re down and yell:&nbsp;

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:51.805
- (Starlight) Eat my sh** you Nazi b****!

00:10:51.805 --> 00:10:55.440
- (Michael) See, in the brand-safe,&nbsp;
virtue-signaling realm of corporate social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.440 --> 00:11:00.080
justice, everything has to “play” well with&nbsp;
a large audience. And so all the corporations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:04.480
who sponsor pride parades want to ignore&nbsp;
that the first “pride” was actually a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:08.720
riot incited by police brutality. Or&nbsp;
how those who vaguely stand against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:13.520
“hate” on Instagram never want to go into&nbsp;
the details about what that actually means.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:19.680
But The Boys does - it looks like this. Three&nbsp;
women giving a bloody beatdown to a literal nazi.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:20.478
- (French) Girls do get it done!

00:11:20.478 --> 00:11:26.000
- (Michael) Also, congrats Marvel, you’ve been&nbsp;
roasted.&nbsp;Now, a common problem with the way the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:31.840
word virtue-signaling gets thrown around is that&nbsp;
the term seems exclusively used against the left.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:36.640
So a sensible question would be: is virtue&nbsp;
signaling confined to the liberal sphere?&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:41.520
And the answer to that is: absolutely not.&nbsp;We&nbsp;
just don’t usually think about it in those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:46.880
terms. To see what I mean, let’s look at the&nbsp;
king of conservative virtue signaling himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:50.640
Homelander.&nbsp;If virtue-signaling is the&nbsp;
invocation of issues or values out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:56.320
self-interest rather than genuine concern,&nbsp;
then this is Homelander’s patriotism to a tee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.320 --> 00:12:01.440
The dude does not give a shit about America,&nbsp;
or American citizens. But he goes to great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.600
lengths to SEEM like he has a raging hard-on&nbsp;
for the troops and the land of the free.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:12.240
- (Homelander) Oh! And you&nbsp;
guys, you, are the real heroes.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:19.040
- (Michael) Not only that, our sociopathic supe&nbsp;
is very careful to invoke all those cheesy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.520
patriotic platitudes when addressing crowds.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:26.720
- (Homelander) And introduce you to a little&nbsp;
thing called God's judgement! That's what I think!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:31.200
Sounds like the American thing to do!

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:32.800
- (Michael) This rhetoric, we might add,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:36.320
is common to all politicians, but&nbsp;
especially those on the right.&nbsp;

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.520
- (Homelander) But if you’ve served&nbsp;
with our amazing soldiers like I have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.600
you’d know that freedom comes at a price.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:48.240
- (Michael) Of course, this is the same guy who&nbsp;
downed a whole airliner of American civilians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.440
before casually flying off and letting them sink&nbsp;
to their watery graves.&nbsp;To see how shallow all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:58.960
this patriotic posturing really is, you need&nbsp;
only to look at what gets Homelander upset:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:03.120
not the deaths of innocent Americans, but&nbsp;
rather those rare moments when he isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:07.680
showered with love and adoration.&nbsp;For&nbsp;
example, when people come after Homelander for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:19.840
accidentally killing an innocent bystander, we&nbsp;
see the strongest man in America break down hard.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:20.768
(Homelander laughs maniacally and cries)

00:13:20.768 --> 00:13:25.440
- (Michael) Of course, Homelander isn’t alone&nbsp;
when it comes to virtue signaling via patriotism.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:31.200
Vought is arguably just as bad.&nbsp; On one hand the&nbsp;
company churns out pro-military ads like this one:

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:35.600
- (Queen Maeve) We’re proud to fly alongside&nbsp;
them.&nbsp;And now we could use your support.&nbsp;

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:39.040
- (Homelander) That’s right, Maeve,&nbsp;
with our new campaign, Saving America.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.960
- (Michael) Sort of like that Captain Marvel ad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:45.600
right? On the other hand, as Stormfront&nbsp;
so rightly points out, it’s all a farce.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.840
- (Stormfront) Oh FYI, not a real base.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:52.480
- (Michael) See, like Homelander, Vought isn’t&nbsp;
interested in actual national security or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:56.880
supporting the troops.&nbsp; All they’re interested&nbsp;
in is those sweet, sweet military contracts.&nbsp;

00:13:56.880 --> 00:14:02.160
- (Madelyn) And there's only one company&nbsp;
that has the product to fight back.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:05.920
- (Michael) And to that end, Vought does&nbsp;
everything from blackmail sitting senators&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:11.040
to imprisoning and experimenting on innocent&nbsp;
civilians with Compound V. Real good job keeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:15.840
America safe. There’s also a kind of Christian&nbsp;
virtue-signaling - you know, pastors who get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:20.400
rich and famous for signaling to the world how&nbsp;
much they love jesus, even if they’re sleezebags.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.360
- (Hughie) He preaches all that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:25.660
"pray the gay-away sh*t.
- (Billy) Nah, he's the meat in the manwich.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:30.240
- (Michael) Like that.&nbsp;And finally there’s&nbsp;
what I’ll call authenticity-signaling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:34.389
which is all about broadcasting how “real”&nbsp;
you are, as best embodied by Stormfront.

00:14:34.389 --> 00:14:39.440
- (Stormfront) Be a bitch if you want! Be&nbsp;
whatever. Just drop the mask once in a while.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:40.640
Feels good.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:44.080
- (Michael) Of course, her&nbsp;
persona is also carefully crafted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:49.440
meant to rile up her base for her own gross ends,&nbsp;
but because she defines herself in opposition to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:54.400
her “squeaky-clean” heroes her own performance&nbsp;
of “realness” finds a receptive audience.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.240
- (Stormfront) As if Homelander and Maeve are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.120
gonna eat in MREs and piss&nbsp;
in a ditch with the rest- &nbsp;

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:04.800
- (Michael) With all this virtue signaling coming&nbsp;
from both the left and right, from individuals to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:10.240
corporations, you might be asking yourself one&nbsp;
simple question: how the fuck did we get here?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:15.520
Virtue signaling, even if it wasn’t called that,&nbsp;
is quite old. They even complain about it in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:21.360
bible, when Jesus said you needed to shut the fuck&nbsp;
up on Facebook about buying a stranger Starbucks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:26.480
Well, I’m paraphrasing, but that’s basically what&nbsp;
he’s saying.&nbsp;But our current virtue-signaling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:32.880
hellscape may be, at least partially, the&nbsp;
result of one industry: public relations, or PR.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:38.240
Ever since Ivy Lee, the founder of modern PR,&nbsp;
first repaired the Rockefeller family’s robber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:43.120
baron image through heavily slanted press releases&nbsp;
and a highly choreographed, sympathy tour through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:48.560
Colorado, the world wised up to the fact that&nbsp;
a little positive publicity goes a long way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:54.640
Of course, people maligned Lee as a “hired&nbsp;
slanderer” and “poisoner of public opinion”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:59.920
and maybe they had a point. Because here’s the&nbsp;
messed up thing, Wisecrack.&nbsp;A hundred years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:04.480
Lee opened up the floodgates, and now the field&nbsp;
of positive spin can be used to rehabilitate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:11.040
the image of just about anyone or anything. And&nbsp;
that’s where things get dark. To see what I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:16.320
let’s look at the messed up journey of the guy&nbsp;
you love to hate: The Deep, aka Aquaman, except he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:21.680
does sexual assault.&nbsp; After being booted from The&nbsp;
Seven for sexually assaulting Starlight, The Deep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:26.480
spirals hard, eventually getting some time in the&nbsp;
clanker for commandeering a kids’ water park.&nbsp;

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:28.400
- (The Deep) You think&nbsp;
water’s supposed to be fun?&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:32.240
Try swimming in the Marianna&nbsp;
trench, you little f****** idiots!

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.920
- (Michael) When he’s bailed out, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:38.080
it’s by the Church of the Collective,&nbsp;
who in exchange for his bank account,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:43.360
agree to do some serious PR work to get him&nbsp;
back into the Seven. To that end, the Church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:49.040
makes the Deep appear in some seriously cheesy&nbsp;
infomercials and even focus tests a wife for him.&nbsp;

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:53.840
- (The Deep) But I thought I got to choose.&nbsp;
- (Woman) You do.&nbsp;And you’re choosing Cassandra.&nbsp;

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:58.880
- (Michael) Now the running joke of the season is&nbsp;
how truly pathetic The Deep is, and how willing he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:04.720
is to go along with a PR blitz that presents such&nbsp;
a patently false image. But underneath the humor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:10.400
we have to realize how fundamentally screwed&nbsp;
up all this is.&nbsp; Through the persuasive dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:15.520
arts of PR, The Deep – a repeat sexual&nbsp;
offender and all around asshole – nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:20.560
regains his position in the most prestigious&nbsp;
paramilitary organization in the world.&nbsp;

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.400
- (Alastair) Did you catch Malala Yousafzai's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:25.040
tweet? Called you a sweetheart!
- (The Deep) Well she's a sweetheart.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:29.920
- (Michael) But if you think it’s terrifying that&nbsp;
PR can rehabilitate a piece of shit like The Deep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:33.920
then you’re going to love this next&nbsp;
one.&nbsp;The Boys shows how PR and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:38.960
its virtue signaling can even make nazism&nbsp;
look kosher.&nbsp;To understand what I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:44.000
let’s look at Homelander and his new boo,&nbsp;
Stormfront.&nbsp;By understanding the ins and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:48.800
outs of PR, Stormfront is able to revitalize&nbsp;
Homelander’s flagging, all American brand.&nbsp;

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:52.320
- (Stormfront) You don’t need 50&nbsp;
million people to love you, you need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:58.880
5 million people f**** pissed.&nbsp;
You have fans.&nbsp; I have soldiers.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:04.000
- (Michael) In other words, Stormfront, in true&nbsp;
Don Draper fashion, knows how to sell a message&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:09.280
to the masses. Basically, Homelander takes all&nbsp;
that patriotic virtue signaling he’s known for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:14.880
and appends it to a violently xenophobic message.&nbsp;
And the results are downright terrifying.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:21.120
- (Homelander) One nation under god,&nbsp;
remember? Right before these godless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:27.360
inhuman supervillains started pouring across&nbsp;
our borders and dragging us down into their mud!

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:30.240
- (Michael) Of course, it goes&nbsp;
without saying that neither&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:35.040
Homelander nor Stormfront cares about this&nbsp;
supposed super terrorist threat.&nbsp;A threat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:38.480
we might add, that was literally&nbsp;
created by Homelander himself.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:43.520
- (Homelander) Did it ever occur to&nbsp;
you that, a sup-terrorist showing up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:50.000
EXACTLY when we needed him to was...&nbsp;
a pretty f**** incredible coincidence?

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:54.320
- (Michael) Instead, all this spin serves&nbsp;
the purpose of a larger, darker message:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.880
a race war led by Eva Braun over here.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:19:01.120
- (Stormfront) They want to wipe us from this&nbsp;
Earth, just because of the color of our skin.&nbsp;

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.840
- (Ryan) Really?
- (Stormfront) It's called white genocide.

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:07.120
- (Michael) See, Stormfront intuitively&nbsp;
understands that if she wants to sell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:10.720
her vision of “white is right,” she&nbsp;
needs to dress it up with all that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.880
classic American apple pie virtue&nbsp;
signaling. Or, in her own words:

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:18.560
- (Stormfront) People love what&nbsp;
I have to say.&nbsp;They believe in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:21.200
it.&nbsp;They just don’t like the word nazi.&nbsp;

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:25.920
- (Michael) It’s also interesting to consider&nbsp;
that Stormfront’s own brand of “realness” is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:30.560
another cynical way to brand herself. While Vought&nbsp;
might traditionally favor the more “buttoned-up”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:35.440
approach of giving speeches with talking points,&nbsp;
she prefers crafting a more unpolished brand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:40.480
but a brand nonetheless:&nbsp;paying people to&nbsp;
make memes and packaging people’s bigotry.

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:43.600
- (Stormfront) Oh this is just the first&nbsp;
batch. I'll have Logan punch up the fear.&nbsp;

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:46.640
- (Homelander) Logan?
- (Stormfront) My meme queen!

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:51.360
- (Michael) Now, the trouble with virtue-signaling&nbsp;
is that many sociologists and philosophers have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:56.160
said that basically EVERYTHING we do is a&nbsp;
performance. Whether you’re going to church,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:59.680
pursuing a career, or getting&nbsp;
a sweet new set of truck nuts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:03.760
everything we do is filtered through how&nbsp;
we think others will perceive our actions.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.160
- (Queen Maeve) But hey, as&nbsp;
long say you're trending right?

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:09.280
- (Michael) If Starlight wants to&nbsp;
do good, and be recognized for it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:13.440
it doesn’t necessarily make her good deeds&nbsp;
worthless. The problem, The Boys wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:17.920
remind us, is when people weaponize good&nbsp;
acts to distract from their evil acts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:22.560
And with a world full of marketers and PR&nbsp;
reps, it’s often hard to tell the difference.&nbsp;

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:27.120
- (Billy) So it's just business then eh?
- (Stan) When, Mr. Butcher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.000
has it ever been about anything different?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.520
- (Michael) But what do you think,&nbsp;
Wisecrack? Is The Boys right? Can we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:37.280
even begin to decipher what’s real&nbsp;
anymore? And does it even matter?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:42.320
Smash that subscribe button like Homelander is...&nbsp;
ok we can’t show that. Don’t forget to ring that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:47.840
bell. Huge thanks to all of our patrons for your&nbsp;
support, and always, thanks for watching, later.&nbsp;

